{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 30, :comments ["<b>For on this day he shall make atonement.</b> The reason you also require, besides this, rest and affliction, is that the priest through his service indeed makes atonement alone, and the nature of atonement is the diminishing of the sin and making it susceptible to forgiveness." "<b>Before HaShem you shall be purified.</b> But the attainment of purification and complete forgiveness shall be before HaShem alone, and this through confession and repentance — He alone knows their truth, and for this reason."], :book :leviticus, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 16, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:36:31.160985764Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}